WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you, everybody.
Thank you so much.

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:07.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
My name is Mike Vecchione.
I'm 100% Italian.

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Thank you. That's never

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:11.277 line:92%
helped me in my life at all.

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:13.079
The only time I tell people
now is when I give blood

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:14.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause they're like,
"What's your blood type?"

00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:19.152
I'm like, "Funny you should ask.
It's 100% Italian."

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:21.721
They're like, "That's not at all
what we mean."

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:25.525
I'm like, "It's what I mean
'cause I want my blood to go

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:29.829
to somebody eating, yelling, or
holding a grudge for no reason."

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:34.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:37.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you. My father had
a gambling problem.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.606
He lost our house when I was 11,
but he didn't come home and say,

00:00:39.606 --> 00:00:41.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I lost the house."
He came home and said,

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:45.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Mike, how would you
like to go camping forever?"

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:48.748 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:49.849 line:92%
There's no help for gamblers.

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:52.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's one sign as you drive
into Las Vegas -- says,

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:55.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Gambling problem?
Please call this number."

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:57.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's ineffective.
It should at least say,

00:00:57.157 --> 00:01:01.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Gambling problem? I bet you
won't call this number."

00:01:01.528 --> 00:01:02.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Thank you,

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:07.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
because these people have
a gambling problem. Thank you.

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:09.769 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:12.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Sighs ] I'm in my 40s,
and, millennials, you're here.

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:16.476
Thank you for being here.
Thank you for paying attention.

00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:19.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know it's really hard
for your people.

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:19.913 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:21.981
You're probably on 12 different
kinds of medications

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:26.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
to make that happen, from the
articles that I've read,

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:30.657
and I know you have tough jobs
as gluten-free web designers

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:38.965 size:84% position:42%
and vegan Uber drivers,
Bitcoin Venmo managers.

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:43.169 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:44.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
There were five jobs I could
have got when I got out

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:48.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
of high school --
five that I could have had.

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:51.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was a band called
the Village People.

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:54.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
Those were your job choices.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:59.385 size:78% position:39%
I was an Indian chief
from 1991 to 1995.

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:00.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's true.

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:06.059 line:92%
That's actually true, everybody.

00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:07.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Sighs ] I think what
I'm talking about

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.629
is diversity, everybody.
That's the name of the game

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:11.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
in show business right now.
It's diversity.

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:13.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
My manager calls me up.
He's like, "Mike, is there

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:16.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
"anything in your background
that could give us

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:19.239 line:92%
some much-needed diversity?"

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:23.076
I'm like, "Well, I'm 100%
Italian. Does that help?"

00:02:23.076 --> 00:02:24.577
He's like, "Actually, that hurts
us a lot,

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:27.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
"So if you could not mention
that again,

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:30.450 line:92%
that would be a big help."

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:33.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's like, "What about what's
going on inside of you?

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:36.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is there any diversity there?"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.456 --> 00:02:41.194
I'm like, "What do you mean?"
He's like, "With your feelings.

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:43.863 size:81% position:41%
Like, sometimes do you
feel like a woman..."

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:45.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
"...that is trapped inside

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:49.569
of a man's body? Because that's
a story we could tell."

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:54.541
I'm like, "No, that's not really
happening."

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:58.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
But I was born C-section.

00:02:58.077 --> 00:03:03.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I was a man who was trapped
inside of a woman's body.

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:04.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter and applause ]
Yeah. Thank you.

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:09.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you, ladies. Thank you.
Thank you.

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:11.524 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:14.127 align:start size:94% position:6%
Guys, we have to be better
to these ladies, okay?

00:03:14.127 --> 00:03:15.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have to be better.
[ Cheering ]

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:20.266
Thank you. We have to be better,
because they deserve it,

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:22.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they will get revenge.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:24.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
I read this article.
The police in Florida found

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:28.541
a severed penis on the side of
the road with a condom on it.

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:32.745
I'm like, wow, that guy was
worried about the wrong things.

00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:35.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Thank you.

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:40.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you, Roots. Thank you.

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:42.689 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:03:42.689 --> 00:03:47.493 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:50.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was the victim
of bad birth order growing up.

00:03:50.597 --> 00:03:53.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was the second-born
male child.

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:54.500 line:92%
My parents had my brother.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're like,
"I guess we're having kids.

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:58.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have a boy.
Let's try for a girl."

00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:02.508
Then they had me. They were
like, "Let's try again."

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:04.911
Then they had my sister.
They're like, "We got it.

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:07.280 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Our boy, and our girl."

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:09.916
[ Laughter ]
"But now we have this extra kid,

00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:12.919
who we can really roll the dice
with, you know?"

00:04:12.919 --> 00:04:14.087 size:75% position:38%
'Cause my father had
a gambling problem.

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:18.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know if I mentioned
that. Pretty sure my father...

00:04:18.358 --> 00:04:21.027 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:22.195 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Thank you.

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:23.630 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:25.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Clears throat ] We had a dog
when I was growing up,

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:29.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the dog used to bite me
occasionally, and now if a dog

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:30.637 line:92%
growls at a kid, he's gone.

00:04:30.637 --> 00:04:35.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
This dog used to bite me...
occasionally.

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:37.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
So I went to my parents.

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:39.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, "Hey,
the dog is biting me."

00:04:39.412 --> 00:04:42.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're like, "We understand
that, but your brother

00:04:42.148 --> 00:04:44.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
